From: Siddhartha Srivastava <siddhartha@delphai.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 22:30:00 +0530
Subject: [PATCH] Rules 2 (testnet run 1 findings): jackpots only for a catch
 on the decoy's wrong stage, directed jobs, challenge bonds scaled to the
 provider's bond, job-op results

- Forced-error record v2 carries a stage key; FEStage(key, job, stages) fixes each decoy's wrong
  stage. Jobs record the stage they failed on (Caught/CaughtStage: games, unserved inputs), and
  FE_REVEAL pays the jackpot (and reimburses the decoy bond) only for a catch on that stage.
- JOB_POST may name the only provider allowed to accept (Job.Directed), so decoys cannot be raced.
- CHALLENGE bonds at least ChallengeBondBP of the provider's bond (testnet: 10%).
- Rules 2 job fields are encoded only when set: replaying the testnet (1329 blocks) gives the
  same state roots. Testnet adopts Rules 2 at height 1400.
- Node: outcomes of recent job ops kept in memory, failures logged, getjobopresult RPC;
  getjob shows catchers, directed provider and caught stage; getjobstate shows the next
  block's rule parameters. uwcctl jobpost takes an optional provider account.

